  "enhanced_information": "The clinical presentation of a 35-year-old woman with maculo-papular lesions, noncaseating granulomas on biopsy, elevated angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) levels, and bilateral hilar adenopathy is highly suggestive of sarcoidosis. According to medical consensus, corticosteroids are the first-line treatment for sarcoidosis, particularly when there are significant symptoms or organ involvement. Other treatment options such as hydroxychloroquine, azathioprine, and leflunomide are generally considered for refractory cases or specific situations but are not standard initial therapies. Therefore, the most appropriate attitude in this case is to start treatment with corticosteroids orally."
